  "releaseNotes": "2.0.5: New \"Partition for arm/disarm, status and HSM\" setting (default 1) for multi-partition panels — status, HSM and arm/disarm keystrokes all use the selected partition. Partition 1 behaves exactly as before; other partitions send keys with the EnvisaLink partition keystroke command. Fixes an addZone error when an interim 2.0.4 development build of the app was paired with the released driver. 2.0.4: Multi-partition panels no longer flap arm status/HSM between partitions — only partition 1 drives the Security Panel and HSM, and a partition's Ready update only closes that partition's zones. Keypad text containing commas is no longer truncated. 2.0.3: Add description text logging preference to all zone drivers. 2.0.2: Fix HSM re-arm feedback loop after disarm via driver-level debounce. 2.0.1: Initial release — native EnvisaLink TPI integration, no SmartThings Node Proxy required.",
